  Done. Four steps, in this order.

  1. MIGRATION 0085, if you haven't already:

         supabase/migrations/0085_listing_favourite_counts.sql

     Then: authenticated may execute it, anon must not.

         select proname, proacl from pg_proc
         where proname = 'listing_favourite_counts';

  2. THE AVATAR BACKFILL — report first, it changes nothing without --apply:

         node tools/backfill-avatar-exif.mjs

     Read the output, then:

         node tools/backfill-avatar-exif.mjs --apply

     If it says orphan deletion was SKIPPED, tell Claude before continuing.

  3. SHIP:

         git checkout -b app-native-complete
         git add -A
         git commit -F - <<'MSG'
Take Selling, Buying, Orders, Rounds and Profile native

The last of the app screens that opened the website now run natively:
Selling, Payouts, Buying, one order from either side, Rounds I've
posted, and Edit profile.

What deliberately still opens the site, in every case because the app
cannot do it rather than because it was easier: paying (Stripe's own
iframe), Stripe Connect onboarding (a hosted redirect whose bank-details
step belongs on Stripe's domain), answering an offer (offer_action(),
0048, is the single write path), and reporting a problem (writes to
reports with the admin client).

Cancelling or deleting a round goes through a new route rather than a
table write. The policy would allow the write; what the app cannot do is
notify everyone who asked, was offered a place, or confirmed one. That
notice is built server-side, so the work moved into
tee-times-operations.ts beside the three writes already there and both
surfaces call it.

Also fixes a live privacy bug: profile photos were uploaded to a public
bucket with EXIF intact, publishing the GPS coordinates of wherever they
were taken. Avatars now go through the same sharp re-encode listing
photos use, and tools/backfill-avatar-exif.mjs cleans the ones already
stored, including orphans left by earlier photo changes.

0085 fixes the saves count, which has always read zero:
listing_favourites is readable only by the member who saved, so a seller
counted nothing. The new SECURITY DEFINER aggregate is scoped by
seller_id, returns counts and never identities, and revokes by name.

The menu loses its Dashboard row — it pointed at a page that repeats,
less well, what the Home tab shows.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
